# layer_norm ci — three dtypes x the row shape, the tail and the optional
# parameter families
#
# Shape column = the case's view: MxNxK with M = rows, N = norm_size,
# K = 1; the params column carries the normalization in the fixed key order
# rows,ns[,e][,sc][,sh] (see tests/inputs/README.md). e is eps scaled by 1e9
# (e0 = 0, e10000 = 1e-5), sc/sh are the use_scale / use_shift flags.
#
# Families covered: the norm_size tail (sizes that are not a multiple of the
# 8-element pack unit and of the vector length: 1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 13, 17, 33,
# 65, 129), the rows scan (1, 2, 3, 5, 8, 17), eps at both ends of the
# corpus range, and all four use_scale x use_shift combinations on the same
# shape so the constant substitution of a missing vector is compared against
# the golden's own substitution.
#
# f32 is bit-exact against the scalar golden; f16/bf16 compare at the dtype
# trait tolerance.
